=== Climate ===
Haruno Prefecture has a tropical monsoon climate (Köppen ''Am''), characterised by extreme rainfall, warm temperatures year-round, and frequent typhoon impacts from the Shendan Ocean. The prefecture is one of the wettest in Okaiken—the interior mountains receive over 4,200 mm of precipitation annually, and the coastal towns regularly experience rainfall events exceeding 200 mm in a single day during the peak typhoon season.

The Shendan Ocean exposure creates a climate that is significantly wetter and more volatile than the Katsuran Sea coast on the western side of Ishijima. The [[Haruno Mountains]] force moist Shendan air upward, creating intense orographic rainfall that sustains the Sea Forest but also produces frequent landslides, flash floods, and coastal erosion. The typhoon season (November–April) is the most dangerous period, with an average of 4–6 typhoon-strength storms making landfall on the Haruno coast each year.

